{
  "Identifier": "f6336fbe-9894-4a69-b5e9-2e774a4e5349",
  "Name": "AGRILINE-TRANFERREPLEN",
  "Description": "AGRILINE-TRANFERREPLEN\n\nIt’s the first half of a two-step restock of the pick faces. A warehouse operator picks a zone, such as ZONE01 or ZONE02, and the system works out which items in that zone are running low. It builds a worklist of what to bring down from the upstairs bulk locations. The operator then scans each item out of its bulk location and moves it to a replenishment staging area. A second process, REPLENISHPUTAWAY, moves it from staging into the pick face.\n\nThe operator doesn’t decide what needs replenishing. The system works that out and tells them what to move.\n\nSelecting a zone in the first step calls Utility_CreateReplenishmentTransfers, which creates a real TRANSFER document (RPL-<zone>-<date>) before any scanning happens. If an open document already exists for that zone it is reused, and any open RPL- documents from earlier days are auto-completed. The demand logic is driven by item optional fields rather than min/max levels. An item becomes a candidate when its pick-zone stock plus all staging stock falls below Yearly Sales ÷ 365 × Replenish Days × Minimum Percentage. The line quantity is the shortfall against the full Yearly Sales ÷ 365 × Replenish Days target. Items are skipped if they have no bulk stock, already sit on an open RPL- line, or are missing Yearly Sales or Replenish Days (Minimum Percentage also matters: if it’s blank, nothing is flagged).",
